(6134180, 902722, 67258, '<td valign="top">That knife is rather menacing!  A good range of tones from black through to white, although I can''t decide if the channel mix you have chosen altogether suits the oranges.</td>', 'That knife is rather menacing!  A good range of tones from black through to white, although I can''t decide if the channel mix you have chosen altogether suits the oranges.', '2010-08-18 14:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134184, 903787, 67258, '<td valign="top">Some interesting textures here, and I can see why you were drawn to photograph this, although in this instance I''m personally not keen on your choice of centered composition.</td>', 'Some interesting textures here, and I can see why you were drawn to photograph this, although in this instance I''m personally not keen on your choice of centered composition.', '2010-08-18 14:10:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134188, 903703, 67258, '<td valign="top">I find this almost uncomfortable to look at, very bright, and rather harsh.  I find the foreground/background blend quite disorientating and adds to my visual discomfort.  I am sure this will appeal to some, just not me.</td>', 'I find this almost uncomfortable to look at, very bright, and rather harsh.  I find the foreground/background blend quite disorientating and adds to my visual discomfort.  I am sure this will appeal to some, just not me.', '2010-08-18 14:13:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134189, 903642, 67258, '<td valign="top">A pleasing set up, but let down by the lighting, and most particularly by the lack of clarity and detail in the textures.</td>', 'A pleasing set up, but let down by the lighting, and most particularly by the lack of clarity and detail in the textures.', '2010-08-18 14:13:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134198, 903213, 67258, '<td valign="top">Been done so, so, so many times before, but despite the lack of originality, it is an aesthetically pleasing photo.  As a technical exercise it really can''t be faulted.</td>', 'Been done so, so, so many times before, but despite the lack of originality, it is an aesthetically pleasing photo.  As a technical exercise it really can''t be faulted.', '2010-08-18 14:23:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134203, 903436, 67258, '<td valign="top">Lovely rendition of textures throughout the photo, and pleasing tones.  Compositionally I would prefer the mallet to be placed a little more to the lower right to make use of some of that empty space.</td>', 'Lovely rendition of textures throughout the photo, and pleasing tones.  Compositionally I would prefer the mallet to be placed a little more to the lower right to make use of some of that empty space.', '2010-08-18 14:27:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134247, 902802, 67258, '<td valign="top">A thoroughly interesting and modern take on the challenge.</td>', 'A thoroughly interesting and modern take on the challenge.', '2010-08-18 15:12:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134263, 903748, 67258, '<td valign="top">I like your idea  and the composition, but feel that there is some way to go with the lighting before this would be truly successful.</td>', 'I like your idea  and the composition, but feel that there is some way to go with the lighting before this would be truly successful.', '2010-08-18 15:18:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6134274, 903118, 67258, '<td valign="top">The compositional structure is fine, but this doesn''t really work for me over-all.  The basket of dried flowers looks messy and bitty, and is quite confusing to the eye - possibly better in colour, and part of the challenge is making the right choices for mono conversion.  The lighting doesn''t really help your photo - side lighting, which you seem to be using is a good choice, but your set-up with the ultra black foreground and background blots out the essential shadows. There seems to be something a bit strange going on with the pear lying in the dish, possibly some JPEG artefact''s from post processing?  All in all, a good effort, but if you repeat the exercise, I feel that you need to concentrate on reproducing textures and shadows.</td>', 'The compositional structure is fine, but this doesn''t really work for me over-all.  The basket of dried flowers looks messy and bitty, and is quite confusing to the eye - possibly better in colour, and part of the challenge is making the right choices for mono conversion.  The lighting doesn''t really help your photo - side lighting, which you seem to be using is a good choice, but your set-up with the ultra black foreground and background blots out the essential shadows. There seems to be something a bit strange going on with the pear lying in the dish, possibly some JPEG artefact''s from post processing?  All in all, a good effort, but if you repeat the exercise, I feel that you need to concentrate on reproducing textures and shadows.', '2010-08-18 15:25:08.000000', NULL, 1),
